#
# Root filesystem profiles for the Raspberry Pi Pico.
#
# distrib/rp2040/mi.rp2040 brackets each optional feature between
# "#closure NAME" and "#endclosure NAME". A profile names the closures and
# groups it keeps; distrib/rp2040/mkmanifest.py emits the base lines plus the
# lines of the named closures and refuses a composition whose hard links,
# parent directories or declared dependencies do not resolve. The Makefile
# variable PROFILE selects one; when it is unset, BOARD picks the default
# (distrib/rp2040/Makefile.inc): full for the PICO board, picocalc for the
# PicoCalc, which names every closure. The Make variables IMAGE_WITH and
# IMAGE_WITHOUT add and remove closures or groups for one build on top of
# the selected profile.
# sys/arch/rp2040/doc/PROFILES.md is the authority for the scheme and
# carries the measured block cost of each closure.
#
# Grammar, one directive per line:
#
#   profile NAME [NAME ...]             a selectable composition
#   group NAME NAME ...                 NAME stands for each listed closure
#                                       or group wherever a closure name is
#                                       taken (profile, IMAGE_WITH, needs)
#   closure NAME needs closure OTHER    OTHER must be selected too
#   closure NAME needs path PATH ...    PATH must reach the image
#   multicall CLOSURE PATH NAME ...     CLOSURE installs the binary PATH that
#                                       dispatches on the names listed; each
#                                       NAME is a closure that links
#                                       dirname(PATH)/NAME to PATH
#   cost NAME BLOCKS INODES             the measured cost of a closure or
#                                       group (see PROFILES.md for the method)
#
# A dependency is checked, never resolved: a profile that names a closure
# without the closure it needs fails the build rather than gaining the
# missing part silently, so the profile line stays the whole statement of
# what an image carries.
#

#
# Groups. A group keeps its old meaning as a profile word: games is the
# gamebox directory, binary and every game linked into it, puzzles is the
# puzzlebox binary and every puzzle, toolchain is the compile chain without
# its link library, calc-bignum is bc with its library and dc.
#
group games gamesdir gamebox fifteen keen bubble fourfall coil
group puzzles puzzlebox flood samegame unruly lightup
group toolchain as ld smlrc cc
group calc-bignum bc dc

#
# Dependencies between closures.
#
# usr.bin/cc runs smlrc, as and ld over a source file and links the result
# against /usr/lib/crt0.o and /usr/lib/libc.a, so a compiler without the
# link library produces an a.out that no stage of the chain can finish.
# The requirement runs both ways: the library is 55 KiB of flash that
# nothing on the board reads once the compiler is gone. The assembler, the
# linker and Smaller C each run on their own, so each is a closure that
# needs nothing; the cc driver needs all three and the library.
#
closure cc needs closure as ld smlrc toolchainlib
closure toolchainlib needs closure cc
closure as needs path /usr/bin/as
closure ld needs path /usr/bin/ld
closure smlrc needs path /usr/libexec/smlrc
closure cc needs path /usr/bin/cc /usr/bin/as /usr/bin/ld
closure cc needs path /usr/libexec/smlrc
closure toolchainlib needs path /usr/lib/libc.a /usr/lib/crt0.o

#
# games/gamebox dispatches on argv[0]; fifteen, keen, bubble, fourfall,
# coil and ridge are hard links to it, and games/puzzlebox does the same for flood,
# samegame, unruly and lightup. Each entry point is a closure of its own
# carrying its link, and the multicall lines below name the members of each
# binary: the games Makefiles link only the selected members into the
# program, and the manifest checker rejects a link whose source the profile
# dropped, a selected member whose binary is absent, and a binary with no
# selected member. The puzzlebox closure installs into /usr/games, which the
# gamesdir closure creates, so an image that leaves the games out keeps the
# puzzles by keeping gamesdir and one that keeps the puzzles names both.
#
multicall gamebox /usr/games/gamebox fifteen keen bubble fourfall coil ridge
multicall puzzlebox /usr/games/puzzlebox flood samegame unruly lightup
closure gamebox needs closure gamesdir
closure gamebox needs path /usr/games/gamebox
closure puzzlebox needs closure gamesdir
closure puzzlebox needs path /usr/games/puzzlebox

#
# usr.bin/bc compiles its input to dc source and evaluates it with the dc
# evaluator linked into bc itself, in a forked child, so bc needs no
# /usr/bin/dc to run, and dc needs nothing of bc. bc -l first reads
# /usr/share/misc/bc.library. The arbitrary-precision calculator ships bc,
# dc and the library together as the calc-bignum group; each is a closure
# an image can keep alone.
#
closure bc needs path /usr/bin/bc /usr/share/misc/bc.library
closure dc needs path /usr/bin/dc

# usr.bin/calc, the scientific calculator with the F-key item bar sized for
# the PicoCalc's 53 by 32 console, is one self-contained program.
#
closure calc needs path /usr/bin/calc

#
# The PicoCalc's SD card is block major 5 and raw major 11 of the PICOCALC
# kernels (sys/arch/rp2040/rp2040/conf.c). The sdcard closure carries the
# /mnt mount point, the nodes for the whole card and its first two
# partitions, and savecore(8), which copies a crash dump off the card's
# dump partition; it needs no other closure, and the PICO board's kernel
# has no driver behind those majors, so only the picocalc profile names it.
#
closure sdcard needs path /mnt /dev/sd0 /dev/sd0a /dev/sd0b /dev/rsd0 /dev/rsd0a /dev/rsd0b /sbin/savecore

#
# The PicoCalc's pixel device is minor 1 of character major 10, the console's
# major, so only the PICOCALC kernels have a driver behind /dev/lcdgfx and
# only the picocalc profile names the closure.
#
closure lcdgfx needs path /dev/lcdgfx

#
# games/ridge is a gamebox member that draws through /dev/lcdgfx (the tile
# atlas and the raw key session of the PICOCALC kernels), so it is outside
# the games group, whose closures the PICO board's image keeps, and it needs
# the device node.
#
closure ridge needs closure lcdgfx

#
# Measured cost. Each line records the free blocks and free inodes an image
# loses when it holds base plus the named closure or group plus the closures
# that name needs, read from `fsutil --verbose --partition=1` on the built
# image; cc and toolchainlib carry one figure because each requires the
# other. gamebox and puzzlebox have no line of their own: a binary with no
# member is refused, so each is measured through a member or its group.
# sys/arch/rp2040/doc/PROFILES.md holds the method, the marginal cost of
# each multicall member inside the full set, and the profile totals.
#
cost coremark 16 1
cost as 25 1
cost ld 18 1
cost smlrc 42 1
cost cc 133 7
cost toolchainlib 133 7
cost toolchain 133 7
cost bc 40 2
cost dc 21 1
cost calc-bignum 60 3
cost calc 33 1
cost sdcard 11 8
cost lcdgfx 0 1
cost gamesdir 1 1
cost games 24 2
cost puzzles 37 2
cost fifteen 8 2
cost keen 10 2
cost bubble 10 2
cost fourfall 15 2
cost coil 8 2
cost ridge 11 3
cost flood 18 2
cost samegame 18 2
cost unruly 21 2
cost lightup 23 2

#
# The compositions.
#
# base       the shell, /etc/rc, the multicall binaries and the editors
# benchmark  base plus CoreMark, for a reported score on a bare board
# developer  base plus the native compile chain and its link library
# games      base plus gamebox and puzzlebox with their nine entry points
#            (the games and puzzles groups)
# full       every closure a bare Raspberry Pi Pico ships; the image the
#            PICO board builds by default
# picocalc   full plus the ClockworkPi PicoCalc's own closures: the
#            arbitrary-precision calculator, the scientific calculator, the
#            SD card's device nodes, the pixel device node and the platformer
#            that draws on it; the PICOCALC board's default
#
profile base
profile benchmark coremark
profile developer toolchain toolchainlib
profile games games puzzles
profile full coremark toolchain toolchainlib games puzzles
profile picocalc coremark toolchain toolchainlib games puzzles calc-bignum calc sdcard lcdgfx ridge
